{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "What the sandboxed RecompLauncher may see. Start from this file:",
    "  cp sandbox/sandbox.json.example ~/.config/recomplauncher/sandbox.json",
    "Then edit the lists and run: sandbox/rl-sandbox",
    "",
    "input/hidraw: controllers. /dev/input is the event device; /dev/hidraw is how SDL reads an",
    "  Xbox pad (and a Bluetooth DualSense comes through uhid). Turn hidraw off to keep the raw HID",
    "  nodes out, or input off for neither.",
    "",
    "read_only  : visible, cannot be written (game folders, disc images, ROM collections).",
    "read_write : visible and writable (where games are installed, save folders).",
    "Nothing else exists inside the sandbox: no other home directories, no SSH keys, no browser",
    "profile, no documents. The launcher's own folders are added automatically unless",
    "auto_dirs is false.",
    "",
    "Checked before you rely on it:  sandbox/rl-sandbox --list",
    "Proven by the test suite:       sandbox/test-sandbox.sh"
  ],

  "binary": "",
  "args": [],

  "network": true,
  "gpu": true,
  "input": true,
  "hidraw": true,
  "sound": true,
  "x11": true,
  "wayland": true,
  "session_bus": true,
  "shared_memory_mb": 8192,
  "auto_dirs": true,
  "webkit_sandbox": false,

  "read_only": [
    "~/Games",
    "/run/media",
    "/media",
    "/mnt"
  ],
  "read_write": [
    "~/Games/Recomp Library",
    "~/.local/share/applications",
    "~/Desktop"
  ],

  "_read_write": [
    "~/.local/share/applications is where the launcher writes a game's menu entry ('Add to the",
    "applications menu'), and ~/Desktop is where it writes the shortcut when you ask for one on the",
    "desktop. Without them the launcher makes neither, and says nothing: it treats a failed write",
    "there as 'no shortcut asked for'. Keep them as the last path, and the folder itself rather than",
    "~/.local/share, so the sandbox doesn't also hand over Steam, Flatpak's exports and the trash."
  ],

  "_optional": [
    "Only uncomment what the launcher really needs. Each line is a path it can then reach.",
    "~/.local/share/Steam        adding games to Steam, and Proton under compatibilitytools.d",
    "~/.steam                    the same, for a Steam installed from the distribution",
    "~/.config/autostart         'Start with your PC' writes its entry here",
    "~/Pictures/RecompLauncher   in-game screenshots",
    "~/Downloads                 if your disc images are there",
    "~/storage/Projects/games/RC.Games   a games folder that isn't under ~/Games"
  ],

  "extra_env": {}
}
